{"id": "EUVD-2026-86683", "enisaUuid": "44e230d8-2f3b-35ba-82d4-f955f13ce9e8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: dsa: bcm_sf2: bound the CFP rule dump by the caller's buffer size\n\nbcm_sf2_cfp_rule_get_all() walks the whole cfp.unique bitmap into\nrule_locs[] without consulting nfc->rule_cnt, which is how many entries\nthe caller had room for.  ETHTOOL_GRXCLSRLALL requires no CAP_NET_ADMIN\nand the ioctl sizes the buffer from the rule_cnt userspace passes in, so\nonce an admin has installed CFP rules any user can ask for fewer slots\nthan there are rules and run off the end of the allocation.  A rule_cnt\nof 0 leaves the buffer pointer NULL and the walk dereferences it.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:12:35", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca49c526291d7cd3a5cb49b0edd7f50a5ae7176e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e41ce02589c92356bfd8ef62f6ceff840546e1a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f2cf4ef2d94fc15fd2e21c131fc1ab3f76125bf4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5e93162b3dd195bfda815e8f7a39aaf1d45437b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f1a2869b3629c0e8394b77b38cb9f19a018c653c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd1a78c16b1f6978c09cf048e15f349732e4c707", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b231b6d8516d3fe0d4bba549908e08d26a4531a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cdb719f4b8596d9ccee2d56d204c2c4dce982f46"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98030", "GHSA-hmh5-2wm8-hhp7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17e83c30-72c3-3737-b491-e610301122d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7318166cacad158b46240f66250d7cc5a481653b <ca49c526291d7cd3a5cb49b0edd7f50a5ae7176e"}, {"id": "253c3971-5535-36b5-a4e9-8c426f6d3175", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "